Third-party material in linog_auto/ (each listed in linog_auto/README.md and linog_auto/selftest_kit/README.md):

1. ISCE2 (https://github.com/isce-framework/isce2), Apache License 2.0, Copyright California
   Institute of Technology. The Apache 2.0 text is in linog_auto/selftest_kit/mock_stack/LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt.
   - selftest_kit/mock_stack/: byte copies of ISCE2's stackStripMap.py, Stack.py, stripmapWrapper.py,
     invertMisreg.py and referenceStackCopy.py (stackStripMap.py and Stack.py from the conda-forge
     isce2 2.6.4 package).
   - selftest_kit/mock_isce/isce/components/isceobj/Sensor/CEOS.py, its db/alos_slc/ record definitions
     (image_file.xml, image_record.xml, leader_file.xml, scene_record.xml) and
     selftest_kit/mock_isce/isce/defaults/logging/logging.conf: byte copies from isce2 2.6.3.
   These copies serve only the self-test's mock environment; a real run uses the installed ISCE2.
   - unpackFrame_ALOS.py (the unpacker the pipeline runs) and its copy selftest_kit/unpackFrame_ALOS.py:
     modified from ISCE2's stripmapStack unpackFrame_ALOS.py; the LInOG changes are in the code.

2. MintPy (https://github.com/insarlab/MintPy), GNU General Public License v3 or later,
   Copyright Zhang Yunjun and Heresh Fattahi.
   - selftest_kit/mock_mintpy/mintpy/defaults/smallbaselineApp.cfg: a copy of MintPy 1.6.2's template.
   - lp_p5.py and selftest_kit/kit3/linog_watermask.py import MintPy.

No data is included: no ALOS-1 PALSAR data (copyright JAXA/METI) and no NAMRIA IfSAR data.
The configuration files (linog_paths.cfg, linog_env.cfg, linog_stack.cfg) carry the authors'
server paths; edit them for another machine. fftw/wisdom_felix.wis is an FFTW plan for that server.
